  "answer": "This feature has been requested before. PowerToys has no timer that shuts down or sleeps the PC after a set number of minutes. Tickets #34919 (sleep after N minutes) and #32852 (scheduled shutdown) were both closed as duplicates of #28490, which is the main request for a shutdown scheduling utility. Add your vote or your use case to #28490. In the meantime, you can use the built-in Windows command `shutdown /s /t <seconds>`. For example, `shutdown /s /t 3600` shuts down after 60 minutes, and `shutdown /a` cancels it. You can put the command in a shortcut (.lnk) or a Task Scheduler task. For sleep, use Task Scheduler or a third-party tool. Related requests are #12191, which asks for a sleep or shutdown action when an Awake period ends, and #15582, which was closed as a duplicate of #12191."
 },
